{"uncertainty": 0.2, "outcome": "rtl_bug", "artifacts": [{"kind": "root_cause_analysis", "title": "Root cause of the uart_tx regression failure: hold register reloaded by a start pulse while busy", "summary": "Requirement [requirement:req-d10c4df532]: investigate and reproduce the failing uart_tx test. Evidence: VeriTriage gave unknown_failure at 30% confidence with a top hypothesis of 'Likely RTL bug' ([evidence:prj-a0b3e1ca75.triage.e1], [run:run-0001]). Icarus reproduced the failure deterministically: 1 of 4 checks failed and $finish was reached at time 546000 ([evidence:prj-a0b3e1ca75.triage.e2], [run:run-0002]). The design under investigation is [artifact:prj-a0b3e1ca75.design-under-investigation.a1], reviewed per [evidence:prj-a0b3e1ca75.design-under-investigation.e1]. Defect: in the non-reset branch the statement `if (start) hold <= data;` sits before and outside the `case (state)`, so it runs in every state, not only IDLE. Causality: the DATA state drives `tx <= hold[bit_idx + 3'd1]` at each bit boundary. A start pulse during a frame therefore replaces `hold` with the new byte, and every data bit after the pulse comes from the new byte. The fault is created at the cycle the stray start is sampled. It becomes visible only at later bit boundaries, so a scoreboard flags the received byte, not the write that corrupted it. Incorrectness: the file's own header contract says 'A start pulse while a frame is in flight is ignored.' Here the pulse is ignored for state sequencing but not for data, which breaks that contract. A fix limited to IDLE (the existing `hold <= data` inside the IDLE branch) would cover every mid-frame timing, not only the failing one. Ranked hypotheses and what would refute each: (1) RTL bug, most likely; it is refuted if the repro below passes on this RTL, or if it also fails on the clean reference RTL. (2) Testbench bug (wrong expectation in the regression test); weakened because the new repro derives its expected bits from the header contract, not from RTL output, and it would be confirmed if the repro failed on clean RTL. (3) Infrastructure; unlikely because the failure reproduced with a clean $finish and a specific 1-of-4 check count, not a crash, timeout or build error ([run:run-0002]); a clean rebuild that made the failure disappear would refute this rejection. (4) Spec ambiguity; rejected because the header states the behaviour explicitly, though one could argue 'ignored' only constrains framing; a spec owner ruling that data reload is allowed would refute this rejection. Limit: the regression log and the upstream triage testbench content are not in my inputs, so I cannot show that the single failed check in [run:run-0002] is this mechanism rather than another one."}], "files": [{"path": "uart_tx_reload_repro_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Minimal self-checking repro: start pulse during a frame must not alter the frame's data bits", "summary": "Repro for [requirement:req-d10c4df532] against [artifact:prj-a0b3e1ca75.design-under-investigation.a1]. It runs four checks, with expected values taken from the 8N1 header contract rather than from RTL output: idle after reset; a clean 0xA5 frame; a 0xA5 frame with a 0x3C start pulse injected during data bit 2, whose bits must still decode as 0xA5; and no second frame after the ignored pulse. On the RTL under investigation, check 3 should fail (bits 3 onward come from 0x3C). On RTL whose hold register only loads in IDLE, all four should pass. It prints exactly one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line, and a watchdog guards against hangs.", "entry": "uart_tx_reload_repro_tb"}], "tool_runs": ["run:run-0001", "run:run-0002"], "claims": ["The clean reference uart_tx presumably differs only by loading hold in IDLE; I have not seen the clean RTL.", "I do not know the exact plusarg name the platform uses to pass the nonce; the testbench tries NIRMAAN_NONCE, nirmaan_nonce, NONCE and nonce. If none matches, the verdict line will carry 'unset' and the gate will not accept it.", "I have not seen the content of triage_report.md, uart_tx_triage_repro.v or regression_fail.log, so I cannot tie the specific failed check in run-0002 to this mechanism."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Expected failing check on the mutant: with 0xA5 sent and the 0x3C reload landing in data bit 2, the decoded byte should be 0x3D (bits 0-2 from 0xA5, bits 3-7 from 0x3C) instead of 0xA5. Inputs are driven and tx is sampled on falling clock edges, mid-bit, to avoid races with the DUT's posedge updates. The testbench does not reference DUT internals. Nothing here has been simulated by me; the platform's simulator.run with expect=fail is the check."}

=== FILE: uart_tx_reload_repro_tb.v ===
// Minimal reproduction: a start pulse while a frame is in flight must be
// ignored (uart_tx header contract), so it must not change the data bits of
// the frame already being sent. Expected values come from the 8N1 contract:
// start bit 0, eight data bits LSB first, stop bit 1, CLKS_PER_BIT cycles each.
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
module uart_tx_reload_repro_tb;
    localparam integer CPB = 4;
    localparam integer T   = 10;

    reg        clk   = 1'b0;
    reg        rst   = 1'b1;
    reg        start = 1'b0;
    reg  [7:0] data  = 8'h00;
    wire       tx;
    wire       busy;

    integer passed = 0;
    integer failed = 0;
    reg [8*128-1:0] nonce;

    reg [7:0] rx_byte;
    reg       rx_start_ok;
    reg       rx_stop_ok;
    reg       quiet_ok;
    integer   n;

    uart_tx #(.CLKS_PER_BIT(CPB)) dut (
        .clk  (clk),
        .rst  (rst),
        .start(start),
        .data (data),
        .tx   (tx),
        .busy (busy)
    );

    always #(T/2) clk = ~clk;

    task check;
        input            cond;
        input [8*48-1:0] name;
        begin
            if (cond) begin
                passed = passed + 1;
                $display("check PASS: %0s", name);
            end else begin
                failed = failed + 1;
                $display("check FAIL: %0s", name);
            end
        end
    endtask

    // Wait for a start bit, then sample each bit at its middle. tx changes on
    // rising edges; the samples land on falling edges.
    task receive;
        integer k;
        begin
            @(negedge tx);
            #(CPB*T/2 + T/2);
            rx_start_ok = (tx === 1'b0);
            for (k = 0; k < 8; k = k + 1) begin
                #(CPB*T);
                rx_byte[k] = tx;
            end
            #(CPB*T);
            rx_stop_ok = (tx === 1'b1);
        end
    endtask

    task pulse;
        input [7:0] d;
        begin
            @(negedge clk);
            start = 1'b1;
            data  = d;
            @(negedge clk);
            start = 1'b0;
            data  = 8'h00;
        end
    endtask

    initial begin
        nonce = "unset";
        if (!$value$plusargs("NIRMAAN_NONCE=%s", nonce))
            if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce))
                if (!$value$plusargs("NONCE=%s", nonce))
                    if (!$value$plusargs("nonce=%s", nonce))
                        nonce = "unset";

        repeat (4) @(negedge clk);
        rst = 1'b0;
        repeat (2) @(negedge clk);
        check((tx === 1'b1) && (busy === 1'b0), "idle line high and not busy after reset");

        // Baseline frame, no interference.
        fork
            receive;
            pulse(8'hA5);
        join
        check(rx_start_ok && rx_stop_ok && (rx_byte === 8'hA5), "clean frame 0xA5 sent LSB first");
        wait (busy === 1'b0);
        repeat (2) @(negedge clk);

        // Frame 0xA5 with a start pulse (data 0x3C) during data bit 2.
        fork
            receive;
            begin
                pulse(8'hA5);
                repeat (13) @(negedge clk);
                pulse(8'h3C);
            end
        join
        $display("mid-frame start: received 0x%02h, expected 0xA5", rx_byte);
        check(rx_start_ok && rx_stop_ok && (rx_byte === 8'hA5), "start while busy leaves frame data 0xA5 intact");

        // The ignored pulse must not launch a second frame.
        wait (busy === 1'b0);
        quiet_ok = 1'b1;
        for (n = 0; n < CPB*12; n = n + 1) begin
            @(negedge clk);
            if ((tx !== 1'b1) || (busy !== 1'b0))
                quiet_ok = 1'b0;
        end
        check(quiet_ok, "ignored start launches no second frame");

        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
        $finish;
    end

    initial begin
        #200000;
        $display("check FAIL: watchdog timeout");
        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed + 1);
        $finish;
    end
endmodule
=== END FILE ===

