is: the same testbench failing on RTL that loads hold only in IDLE. (3) infrastructure, rejected because triage [evidence:prj-a0b3e1ca75.triage.e2] reports a deterministic failure with $finish reached and a counted failed check, not a build or tool error. What would refute this: a clean rebuild with no other change that passes. (4) spec_ambiguity, rejected because the header clause fixes the behaviour explicitly. What would refute this: a governing specification that allows a mid-frame start to update the payload. PROPOSED FIX, not applied here: delete the unconditional `if (start) hold <= data;`. The IDLE branch already loads hold when a frame starts. Then add an assertion that hold is stable while busy."}], "files": [{"path": "uart_tx_reload_repro_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Minimal self-checking repro: a start pulse during a frame must not alter the frame's data bits", "summary": "This testbench checks the header contract of [artifact:prj-a0b3e1ca75.design-under-investigation.a1], that a start pulse during a frame is ignored. It sends a clean 0xA5 frame, then a 0xA5 frame with a 0x3C start pulse during data bit 2. It samples each bit at its middle and expects 0xA5, a value derived from the 8N1 contract. It then checks that the ignored pulse launches no second frame. It prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line. On the RTL under investigation it is expected to report 3 passed, 1 failed (0x3D received), matching the 1-of-4 failure pattern in [evidence:prj-a0b3e1ca75.triage.e2]. On RTL that loads hold only in IDLE it is expected to pass.", "entry": "uart_tx_reload_repro_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["Hand analysis of the timing in the RTL under investigation predicts that the mid-frame-start frame arrives as 0x3D instead of 0xA5. No simulation was run by me.", "The repro is expected to pass on RTL whose hold register loads only in IDLE. This has not been run.", "The nonce plusarg name is not given in my inputs. The testbench tries NIRMAAN_NONCE, nirmaan_nonce, NONCE and nonce in that order."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Attempt 1 was refused for listing tool runs that were never recorded. This attempt lists no tool runs and does not claim any tool execution. The reproduction run with expect=fail is left to the platform, over uart_tx_reload_repro_tb.v plus the approved RTL. Independent review is still required. The design-under-investigation review [evidence:prj-a0b3e1ca75.design-under-investigation.e1] covers the RTL fixture, not this analysis. Remaining uncertainty: I cannot see the regression testbench behind the original failure. If its failing check is something other than mid-frame reload, this diagnosis covers the repro but may not explain that check."}
